# =============================================================================
# experiment/molaro/molaro_T-20_h1.00_8h_a1.34e-2_dirichlet.opts
#
# Molaro -20 C pair, open boundaries at FULL saturation. Pair with
# geometry/molaro/molaro_2D_L382um_eps0.35um_axisym_T-20pair_r0p22.opts.
#
# Middle arm of a three-way boundary comparison, all otherwise identical:
#   molaro_T-20_h1.00_8h_a1.34e-2.opts            sealed (zero-flux)
#   molaro_T-20_h1.00_8h_a1.34e-2_dirichlet.opts  THIS — open, h = 1.000
#   molaro_T-20_h0.998_8h_a1.34e-2_dirichlet.opts open, h = 0.998 (calibrated)
#
# WHY THREE
# ---------
# The three arms separate two effects that the old campaign varied together.
# Going sealed -> open at h = 1.000 changes ONLY the boundary type: it gives
# the latent heat a sink and stops the vapour reservoir depleting, without
# changing the thermodynamic state the walls are held at (at humidity 1.00 and
# uniform T the pinned rho_v IS the equilibrium value, so nothing is injected).
# Going h = 1.000 -> 0.998 then changes only the chamber state.
#
# Molaro's chamber is a sealed Peltier cryostage with the grains sitting on a
# glass slide over the cold plate and an ice-coated slide nearby as a vapour
# reservoir. Neither idealisation is exactly it: zero-flux walls 20 um away
# give the latent heat nowhere to go, while Dirichlet walls 20 um away are an
# infinite reservoir far closer than the real one. The two BRACKET the real
# chamber -- report them that way rather than calling either one correct.
#
# WHAT TO READ OFF
# ----------------
# The EXPONENT, not the rate. If it is insensitive to the boundary treatment
# across all three arms, then the finding that this geometry cannot resolve a
# power law (studies/sinter_exponent/README.md) is a property of the grain
# size and eps, not an artifact of how the box was closed -- which is the
# claim the Demmenie comparison rests on.
#
# Everything else is identical to the sealed arm: t_final 8 h, alpha_c
# 1.341e-2 from the repo Arrhenius fit, beta_sub0 and d0_sub0 from comp_eps at
# -20 C, dtmax 1.0e2 (~1.03 * tau_sub), log-spaced output.
#
# Exclude the first ~2000 s from any fit: the union IC's crease has to build a
# 2.19 um fillet first (t_fill ~ beta*rho^2/(2*d0) = 1400 s). Use --tmin 2000.
#
# Mass is not conserved with -flag_BC_rhovfix 1, so TOTAL_MASS drift in the
# monitor table is expected and is not a solver fault. At h = 1.000 it should
# be small; if it is not, the sealed arm was starved and that is itself the
# result.
# =============================================================================

-t_final 2.88e4                         # 8 h

-temp -20.0
-humidity 1.00                          # walls at ice saturation
-grad_temp0 0.0,0.0,0.0

-flag_BC_Tfix 1                         # isothermal reservoir (the cold plate)
-flag_BC_rhovfix 1                      # rho_v pinned at hum0 * rho_vs(T)

-beta_sub0 5.9216e5                     # K&P beta0 at -20 C, alpha_c = 1.341e-2
-d0_sub0 1.0166e-9                      # physical capillary length at -20 C

-dtmax 1.0e2
-dtCFL 1
-dtCFL_dphimax 0.2

-t_out_log 60
